A||N||5||jackson||Clutch chatter - Dogbone||||1||
Z||000000||jackson||02-03-2001||01:03 PM||||My 88 V6 had a little bit of chatter whenever the clutch wasn't released just properly. Since the clutch is new I knew that wasn't it. I checked the motor mounts and they were fine. Finally, I looked at the dogbone and it had a tiny bit of play. So I removed the dogbone bolt, wrapped it with a few rounds of electrical tape and put it back in. Now it's snug and the chatter is gone! A nice & easy ten minute fix. If it comes again I'll replace the bushing or maybe try a slightly larger diameter bolt.||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||02-03-2001||01:07 PM||||Is this a stock or aftermarket strut? Wrapping tape on that bolt should not make any diferance on a stock strut. If it is properly tightened the sleeve clamps against the bracket. No way for it to move. <P>This should also be true of aftermarket struts if they are properly designed. Some aftermarket struts appear to have a core sleeve that may be a little short and because of it people aren't getting proper clamping.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 02-03-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||jackson||02-03-2001||01:23 PM||||It's a stock dogbone. And it was very tightly bolted in. After removing I could see that the bolt was very loose in the bushing. I can't see how this can get snug without adding material because the ears the bolt goes through do not compress the bushing.||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||02-04-2001||12:57 PM||||What you are saying then is you wrapped the inner sleeve with tape, not the bolt itself. Wrapping the sleeve would tighten a bushing up. Wrapping the bolt would not.||||reg||1
Z||000004||jackson||02-04-2001||01:20 PM||||I think we're getting to a point of understanding on this. I wrapped the non-threaded portion of the bolt w/ tape. Then tapped it through the bushing and tightened the nut. This is the same as if I had wrapped the inside of the bushing sleeve. Like I said before - no more chatter. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||mope||02-04-2001||09:12 PM||||i think you confused everyone more than helped...i understood but it doesnt seem like anyone else did. or maybe its just cuz im crazy i understand crazy people<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>m0pe||||reg||12
